From 218e3f8550ba11288155885b78bb9c67f0541769 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roberto Dantas <address-in-upstream-commit@localhost>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:16:50 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: tipd: sn201202x: probe asynchronously

Renegotiating an inherited connection waits about 5.6 s per port, and
the controllers of one machine probed one after another, so with three
ports in use the last one came up after 17 s. Prefer asynchronous
probing; the driver keeps no shared state besides the debugfs root,
which is already locked.

On a J575c with three inherited connections all three are renegotiated
within 2 ms of each other, 13.8 s after boot instead of 25.1 s.

Assisted-by: LLM (Claude Code)
Signed-off-by: Roberto Dantas <address-in-upstream-commit@localhost>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
Upstream: aurora-silicon/linux commit 218e3f8550ba11288155885b78bb9c67f0541769, pull request 1671
(merged 2026-11-13, after the installed base a34d26c255c2). License GPL-2.0. Unchanged except that
the author's e-mail address is replaced here; the upstream commit has it. Applies to the installed
source with an offset of 10 lines. OPTIONAL for the K114s: see docs/r3-usb.md, it is not a fix.

 drivers/usb/typec/tipd/spmi.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/spmi.c b/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/spmi.c
index 30d472c3d83a..44d1f12a10e8 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/spmi.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/spmi.c
@@ -985,6 +985,11 @@ static struct spmi_driver sn201202x_driver = {
 		.name = "sn201202x",
 		.pm = &sn201202x_pm_ops,
 		.of_match_table = sn201202x_of_match,
+		/*
+		 * Renegotiating an inherited connection waits several seconds per
+		 * port; let the ports of one machine probe at the same time.
+		 */
+		.probe_type = PROBE_PREFER_ASYNCHRONOUS,
 	},
 	.probe = sn201202x_probe,
 	.remove = sn201202x_remove,
